						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c4cefcf elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="c4cefcf" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<h3><strong>What is Acrylic &amp; How it makes water features amazing?</strong></h3><p>Acrylic is a form of tough plastic with half the weight of glass. It comes in colored or transparent form. Midwest Tropical houses one of the most diverse and spectacular Acrylic water features found anywhere else in the market. Keep scrolling to find ‘<em>the ONE’ </em>for you<em>!</em></p><p><em> </em></p><p><strong>What makes acrylic water features a smart choice?</strong></p><p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>Weather Resistance – Retains Color</strong></p><p style="padding-left: 40px;">Acrylic has great weather-resistance and light-refracting capacities. When it comes to outdoor features, acrylic holds up indefinitely and resist weathering, protecting the colors. Acrylic paints have been known to be unaffected by light, so they retain their color. For indoor features, acrylic makes them easily lit due to its clarity and refractive capacities.</p><p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>Lighter than Glass</strong></p><p style="padding-left: 40px;">Acrylic weighs 50% less than glass, making it easier to handle. Combine this property of acrylic with easy molding into a variety of shapes – you have a recipe for a spectacular water feature that is sparkling, lightweight, clear and exudes professionalism and serenity wherever it is placed.</p><p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>Highly Transparent</strong></p><p style="padding-left: 40px;">Acrylic preserves its optical clarity and doesn’t get yellow with age, retaining its transparency. Resistant to UV light, this material is perfect to be used in a water feature that will be placed outdoors or will be getting significant sunlight exposure indoors.</p>								</div>
